- `0755` (4 digits) means "set permissions to 0755, don't touch special bits"
- `04755` (5 digits) means "set permissions to 0755 AND set setuid"
- `00755` (5 digits) means "set permissions to 0755 AND clear setuid"

For a new directory (starting from 0755 & ~umask with no special bits), both interpretations give the same result for the permission bits. The special bits are 0 either way.

